    "id": "osi-saf-430-sea-ice-concentration-interim",
    "stac_version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The OSI-430-b Global Sea Ice Concentration Interim Climate Data Record provides operational continuation of the OSI-450-a CDR from 2016 to present at 10 km resolution. This product maintains the same algorithm and processing chain as OSI-450-a to ensure temporal consistency across the full time series. Daily sea ice concentration fields are produced with latency suitable for climate monitoring (typically within 1-2 days). The dataset uses SSMIS and AMSR2 brightness temperatures with the same quality control, uncertainty quantification, and masking procedures as the base CDR. For Southern Ocean applications, this product provides near-real-time sea ice concentration data with climate-quality processing, making it suitable for both operational monitoring and extending climate time series. The product includes concentration values, uncertainty estimates, and comprehensive quality flags. When combined with OSI-450-a, users have access to a homogeneous 46+ year sea ice concentration record (1979-present) optimized for Antarctic climate studies.",
